--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -11,3 +11,8 @@ Each task has a stable string `id`, unique within its list and preserved when th
 edited. Use `get(id)` to retrieve a task by ID. `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag`
 and `remove` accept either an ID or a title; IDs take precedence when a reference matches both.
 These methods return a `Result`, with a `not-found` error when the task does not exist.
+
+Every task has `createdAt` and `updatedAt` as ISO-8601 date-time strings in UTC. Both are set to the
+same time when the task is added. Completing, reopening, renaming, tagging or untagging a task updates
+`updatedAt` and preserves `createdAt`. Failed operations and edits that change nothing preserve both
+timestamps.
